     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">For posterity, the solution is to include the offset as if it is a predictor in the conditions argument of marginal_effects. E.g.<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">plot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">marginal_effects</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> scale</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;linear&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;fitted&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                      conditions</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data_frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">b</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><div><br>On Monday, 9 April 2018 21:35:46 UTC+9:30, Lukasz Wiklendt  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Is there a way to remove the offset from the marginal_effects function (or fitted function)?<br>The following code does a simple regression with poisson family with log-rate of 0.5 + 2 * a + b, with a in {0, 1} and b some random offset:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">brms</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tidyverse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">set</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">180409</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>icpt </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>n </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data_frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rbinom</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>df$b </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> exp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mean </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sd </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>df$y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rpois</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> exp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">icpt </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> df$a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df$b</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>df$a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df$a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(!</span><span style=\"color:#000\">exists</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;fit&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> brm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</spa